# Wallpaper plugins that are known to animate, one plugin id per line.
#
# The detector reads this to REPORT what is animating on screens that do
# not show ours. It reports only: nothing automatic acts on it. The audio
# spectrum always runs (about 2.4% of a core against a video wallpaper's
# 3-19% of the GPU), so there is nothing to stop and no reason to.
#
# The manual performance mode reads this too, to know which wallpapers to
# swap out for the still one while a game or a render owns the GPU -- and
# to put exactly those back afterwards.
#
# This is your statement about your own desktop, so it is yours to edit.
# Add a line when you install something that animates. This list is only
# for the ones we cannot make cooperate: a third-party animated wallpaper
# can read the published yield signal directly and yield on its own,
# which is the contract in docs/CONTRATTO-resa.md.

# Video wallpaper. Decodes a file continuously.
luisbocanegra.smart.video.wallpaper.reborn

# Static and near-static, listed so the reasoning is visible rather than
# implied. A single photograph costs nothing after the first paint, and
# org.kde.potd and org.kde.slideshow change at most hourly or daily.
# org.kde.image
# org.kde.color
# org.kde.potd
# org.kde.slideshow
# org.kde.tiled
# org.kde.hunyango
